    {
      "fileName": "junk-tinker.json",
      "id": "YMKtEoNwHKA713Cx",
      "name": "Junk Tinker",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "YMKtEoNwHKA713Cx",
        "folder": "QNG8azRxjOSDbz8x",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Junk Tinker",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You can make useful tools out of even twisted or rusted scraps. When using the Crafting skill to Craft, you can make level 0 items, including weapons and armor, out of junk. This reduces the Price to one-quarter the usual amount but always results in a shoddy item. Shoddy items normally give a penalty, but you don't take this penalty when using shoddy items you made (nor does the worse check penalty of shoddy armor you made apply to you).</p>\n<p>You can also incorporate junk to save money while you Craft any item. This grants you a discount on the item as if you had spent 1 additional day working to reduce the cost, but the item is obviously made of junk. At the GM's discretion, this might affect the item's resale value depending on the buyer's tastes.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "goblin"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
      "category": "ancestry"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "phantom-visage.json",
      "id": "RFzYrKP3eR3WG6hV",
      "name": "Phantom Visage",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "RFzYrKP3eR3WG6hV",
        "folder": "QNG8azRxjOSDbz8x",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Phantom Visage",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You cloak yourself in illusions to mask your nature. Your Phantom Visage is a specific alternate form of a Small or Medium humanoid ancestry prevalent where you grew up (typically human), though it doesn't need to have analogous physical features to your natural goblin form. Your Phantom Visage counts as setting up a disguise for the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Impersonate] use of Deception. If you use any unarmed attacks you gained from a goblin heritage or ancestry feats while in your Phantom Visage, the illusion immediately breaks. You can maintain your Phantom Visage indefinitely, and you can shift back to your true goblin form by using this action again.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "dokkaebi goblin heritage"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Lost Omens Tian Xia Character Guide"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "goblin",
              "illusion",
              "occult",
              "visual"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
      "category": "ancestry"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "rough-rider.json",
      "id": "GF9kkULUYowgjEWM",
      "name": "Rough Rider",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "GF9kkULUYowgjEWM",
        "folder": "QNG8azRxjOSDbz8x",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Rough Rider",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "ancestry",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You are especially good at riding traditional goblin mounts. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Ride] feat, even if you don't meet the prerequisites. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to Nature checks to use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Command an Animal] on a goblin dog or wolf mount.</p>\n<p>If you gain a wolf as an animal companion, it gains the mount special ability (and if you gain an ability that grants you an animal companion with the mount special ability, you can choose a wolf).</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core"
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "key": "GrantItem",
              "uuid": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Ride"
            },
            {
              "key": "FlatModifier",
              "predicate": [
                "action:command-an-animal",
                {
                  "or": [
                    "target:goblin-dog",
                    "target:wolf"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "selector": "nature",
              "type": "circumstance",
              "value": 1
            }
          ],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "goblin"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
      "category": "ancestry"
    },
    {
